---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';import {planets} from '../../lib/planets.mjs';
export function getStaticPaths(){return planets.map(p=>({params:{slug:p.id},props:{p}}));}const {p}=Astro.props;const earth=planets[2];
---
<Layout title={`${p.name} Facts, Size, Orbit & Gravity`} description={p.description} section="Planets"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/planets/">Planet atlas</a> / {p.name}</div><div class="planet-detail"><div><span class="eyebrow">{p.kind} / World 0{planets.indexOf(p)+1}</span><h1>{p.name}</h1><h2>{p.tag}</h2><p>{p.description}</p><a class="btn" href={`/labs/orbit-simulator/?a=${(p.distance/149.5978707).toFixed(3)}&e=${p.e}&mass=1&phase=0`}>Explore this orbit ↗</a></div><img src={`/images/${p.id}.webp`} alt={`${p.name}, NASA and mission partners`} width="1024" height="576"/></div><p class="worked">Image: {p.credit}. Processed mission imagery; apparent color varies with filters and processing.</p><div class="stats-grid"><div class="stat"><span>Equatorial diameter</span><strong>{p.diameter.toLocaleString('en-US')} km</strong></div><div class="stat"><span>One orbit</span><strong>{(p.period/365.25).toFixed(2)} years</strong></div><div class="stat"><span>Distance from Sun</span><strong>{(p.distance/149.5978707).toFixed(2)} AU</strong></div><div class="stat"><span>Solar day</span><strong>{p.day.toLocaleString('en-US')} hours</strong></div></div><div class="explanation"><div><h2>{p.name} compared with Earth</h2><p>Its equatorial diameter is <strong>{(p.diameter/earth.diameter).toFixed(2)} times</strong> Earth’s. Its mass is <strong>{(p.mass/earth.mass).toFixed(2)} times</strong> Earth’s, while its orbital period is <strong>{(p.period/earth.period).toFixed(2)} Earth years</strong>.</p><p>The reference gravity is about <strong>{p.gravity} m/s²</strong>. These rounded values include the reference conventions used in NASA’s fact sheet; the ideal spherical gravity calculator can differ slightly.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/">NASA reference data ↗</a></p></div><aside class="note"><span class="eyebrow">One thing to remember</span><h3>{p.fact}</h3><p>Explore the atlas one planet at a time, or jump into a lab to discover the physics behind the numbers.</p></aside></div><Faq items={[[`How far is ${p.name} from the Sun?`,`${p.name} has a mean orbital distance of about ${p.distance.toLocaleString('en-US')} million kilometers, or ${(p.distance/149.5978707).toFixed(2)} AU. Its actual distance varies through its elliptical orbit.`],[`How long is a year on ${p.name}?`,`An orbit takes approximately ${p.period.toLocaleString('en-US')} Earth days. The orbit simulator lets you see how distance affects the length of a year.`]]}/></div></Layout>
